  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Elections were held in the United States on November 3, 2026, during the second term of Republican president Donald Trump.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383861407:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "According to the article, the department sought a Supreme Court injunction on November 2, 2026, to keep up to 20,000 mail-in ballots in California apart.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383861407:132"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The war with Iran became a subject of Democratic campaigning ahead of the November 3 midterm elections.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383861407:147"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Of 35 Senate races this year, Democrats won 20 and Republicans 13, with 2 not yet called.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:the-senate-table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:31Z",
      "text": "Democrats gained seats in Iowa, North Carolina, Kansas, Maine, Ohio, South Carolina and Texas.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-ia",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-nc",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-ks",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-me",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-oh-special",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-sc",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-tx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:39Z",
      "text": "Of 36 governor's races this year, Democrats won 22 and Republicans 12, with 2 not yet called.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:45Z",
      "text": "Democrats gained governorships in Georgia, Iowa, Nevada, Ohio and Texas.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-ga",
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-ia",
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-nv",
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-oh",
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-tx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:53Z",
      "text": "In the House, Democrats hold 251 seats and Republicans 153, with 31 still to be called, and 218 seats make a majority.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-house-of-representatives-elections:house-infobox"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:59Z",
      "text": "On the map, 41 districts changed party, and 49 are not yet called in the race tables.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-house-of-representatives-elections:house-table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:07Z",
      "text": "Readers also looked up United States midterm election (131,229), James Talarico (62,655), and 2026 United States Senate elections (61,876).",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:United_States_midterm_election:2026-11-02",
        "views:en:James_Talarico:2026-11-02",
        "views:en:2026_United_States_Senate_elections:2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:16Z",
      "text": "On 2 November 2026, 201,102 people read about the article, about 8 times the usual level.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_United_States_elections:2026-11-02",
        "views:en:2026_United_States_elections:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:22Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 10 languages, and after English, the most readers were in Persian, with 26,718.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_United_States_elections:2026-11-02",
        "views:fa:انتخابات_۲۰۲۶_ایالات_متحده_آمریکا:2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:01:28Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers, and a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:fa:انتخابات_۲۰۲۶_ایالات_متحده_آمریکا:2026-11-02",
        "views:pt:Eleições_nos_Estados_Unidos_em_2026:2026-11-02",
        "views:fr:Élections_de_2026_aux_États-Unis:2026-11-02",
        "views:zh:2026年美國選舉:2026-11-02",
        "views:it:Elezioni_parlamentari_negli_Stati_Uniti_d'America_del_2026:2026-11-02",
